[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 986,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 951,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150272,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 951,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma of the liver is a malignant hepatic neoplasm composed of undifferentiated mesenchymal cells.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 987,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 952,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150273,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 952,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>89910/3 Embryonal sarcoma</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 988,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 953,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150274,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 953,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2B5Y &amp; XH42Q2 &amp; XA5DY0 Embryonal sarcoma of liver</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 989,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 954,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150275,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 954,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> undifferentiated embryonal sarcoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> malignant mesenchymoma of the liver.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 990,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 955,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150276,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 955,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 991,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 956,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150277,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 956,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma usually arises in the right hepatic lobe {208754;24210186}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 992,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 957,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150278,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 957,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Patients often present with abdominal distension, pain, fever, and weight loss; hepatic rupture with haemoperitoneum is uncommon {208754}. Leukocytosis and elevated serum alkaline phosphatase are common. Invasion of the inferior vena cava with extension to the right atrium may be observed {1702267}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 993,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 958,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150279,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 958,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma is rare, although it is the most commonly described primary hepatic sarcoma in children. In reported cases, patients were typically aged 5&ndash;15&nbsp;years, with no sex predilection {208754;27781381}; presentation in adulthood is rare {18361435}. Embryonal sarcoma has been reported in association with Li&ndash;Fraumeni syndrome {1702267}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 994,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 959,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150280,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 959,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma is sporadic. Rarely, transformation from mesenchymal hamartoma has been reported {20925497}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 995,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 960,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150281,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 960,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Undifferentiated embryonal sarcoma of the liver harbours alterations in the large microRNA cluster C19MC, just like mesenchymal hamartoma of the liver {17311249}. The most common alteration is t(11;19)(q13;q13.4), leading to <em>MALAT1</em>::C19MC fusion {24120702}, and this fusion drives overexpression of C19MC microRNAs {32310940}. In contrast to mesenchymal hamartoma, embryonal sarcoma uniformly harbours complex copy-number alterations, as well as <em>TP53</em>mutations in 90% of cases {11376805;20925497;32310940}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1002,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 967,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150282,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 967,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma is well circumscribed but unencapsulated. Tumours are large (100&ndash;300&nbsp;mm). The cut surface is heterogeneous, with alternating solid, fleshy, and mucoid areas and foci of cystic degeneration, necrosis, and haemorrhage {208754}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 996,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 961,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150283,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 961,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The tumour is typically composed of variably spindled, stellate, and pleomorphic giant cells loosely arranged in a myxoid stroma; fibrotic areas with solid, fascicular, or storiform growth may be observed {208754;1702267}. Cytoplasmic PAS-positive eosinophilic hyaline (lysosomal) globules in giant cells are a characteristic finding {208754}. Mitotic activity is easily detected, including atypical mitoses. Peripheral entrapment of bile ducts is often seen, as is extramedullary haematopoiesis. Association with mesenchymal hamartoma has been documented {8066077;9331300;11779051;20925497}.</p>\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma shows no specific immunophenotype. Variable, often limited expression of keratins, desmin, and MSA may be seen {1702267;17378682;16785789}; a subset of cases are positive for glypican-3 (GPC3) {21937079}. The tumour cells are negative for EMA, HepPar1 (CPS1), AFP, myogenin, and MYOD1 {17378682}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 997,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 962,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150284,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 962,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Cytology specimens show spindle cells, some of which exhibit marked nuclear pleomorphism {38226775}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 998,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 963,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150285,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 963,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma uniformly shows a complex karyotype and complex copy-number alterations {11376805;32310940}. The t(11;19)(q13;q13.4) characteristic of mesenchymal hamartoma has been detected in several cases {17311249}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1001,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 966,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150286,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 966,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> spindled, stellate, and pleomorphic giant cells loosely arranged in a myxoid stroma.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 999,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 964,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150287,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 964,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1000,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 965,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 150288,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 185,
        "headingId": 965,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Although embryonal sarcoma of the liver may pursue an aggressive clinical course, with metastases to the lung and peritoneum, patients with surgically resectable tumours often have a favourable outcome {24210186;26925712;27427850;38556718;38567652}. Tumour size &gt;&nbsp;150&nbsp;mm is an adverse prognostic indicator {27781381}.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]